# Deploy — project-db on Cloudflare D1

This directory is the MCP Worker for the **{{PROJECT_NAME}}** project database. `/db:publish` regenerates
`../d1/import.sql` from the local SQLite build and pushes it to D1; the Worker serves read-only MCP tools
(`db_query`, `db_schema`, `db_search`) over that database.

## One-time setup

```bash
cd .claude/db/worker
npm install
npx wrangler login                                  # opens a browser; or set CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
npx wrangler d1 create {{DATABASE_NAME}}            # copy database_id into wrangler.toml (publish does this)
npx wrangler secret put MCP_BEARER_TOKENS           # comma-separated tokens; Worker refuses requests until set
```

## Publish data (what /db:publish runs)

```bash
python3 ../db.py sync
python3 ../db.py export-d1                          # writes ../d1/import.sql — no BEGIN/COMMIT, statements < 100 KB
npx wrangler d1 execute {{DATABASE_NAME}} --remote --file=../d1/import.sql --yes
npx wrangler deploy                                 # first time, or after editing src/index.ts
```

Test the import locally first (Miniflare, no account needed):

```bash
npx wrangler d1 execute {{DATABASE_NAME}} --local --file=../d1/import.sql --yes
npx wrangler d1 execute {{DATABASE_NAME}} --local --command "SELECT type, COUNT(*) FROM pages GROUP BY 1"
```

## Verify

```bash
WORKER_URL="https://project-db-{{SLUG}}.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev"
curl -fsS "$WORKER_URL/health"
curl -fsS -X POST "$WORKER_URL/mcp" -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"db_query","arguments":{"sql":"SELECT type, COUNT(*) AS n FROM pages GROUP BY 1"}}}'
```

## Connect a client

Claude Code (`.mcp.json` or `claude mcp add`): type `http`, URL `$WORKER_URL/mcp`, header `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.

## Limits that matter

| Limit (D1) | Value | How project-db copes |
|---|---|---|
| SQL statement length | 100 KB | export batches rows to < 90 KB; cells > 60 KB are appended in chunks |
| Database size | 500 MB free / 10 GB paid | export warns above 500 MB |
| Query timeout | 30 s | Worker caps rows; write narrow queries |
| Bound parameters | 100 | tools bind ≤ 2 |

D1 supports FTS5, views and JSON functions, so the schema is identical to the local file. There is no
read-only role in D1: the Worker's validator + bearer token **are** the read-only role. Rotate tokens with
`wrangler secret put MCP_BEARER_TOKENS`.
